<p class="risk wrap">Every dental treatment carries some risk, and results vary from person to person. Your dentist will explain the benefits, risks and alternatives before any treatment begins.</p>
<section class="dbody land-body">
  <div class="wrap dbody__in">
    <div>
      <h2 data-reveal>What are braces?</h2><p data-reveal>Braces use small brackets and a wire to move teeth slowly. Pearlecent offers several types: metal braces, ceramic and crystal braces that are tooth-coloured or clear, lingual braces that sit behind the teeth, and Damon or self-ligating braces. Clear aligners, such as Invisalign, are a series of clear trays that you can take out.</p><p data-reveal>Each option has its own benefits and limits. The right choice depends on your teeth, your bite and your daily routine. Orthodontic treatment at Pearlecent is planned by <a class="link-u" href="../dentists/ankur.html">Dr. Ankur Agarawal, Orthodontic Specialist</a>.</p>
      <h2 class="land-h2" data-reveal>Who is it for?</h2><p data-reveal>Braces may help teens and adults who have crowded teeth, gaps, teeth that stick out, or a bite where the top and bottom teeth do not meet well.</p><p data-reveal>Adults can have braces too. Your teeth and gums need to be healthy before treatment starts, so the dentist may suggest a <a class="link-u" href="dental-checkup-deira.html">check-up</a> or a <a class="link-u" href="teeth-cleaning-deira.html">cleaning</a> first.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="dfocus">
      <figure class="land-pic" data-reveal><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="../assets/img/treatments/orthodontics-600.webp?v=15 600w, ../assets/img/treatments/orthodontics-1200.webp?v=15 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 48em) 92vw, 520px"><img src="../assets/img/treatments/orthodontics-1200.jpg?v=15" srcset="../assets/img/treatments/orthodontics-600.jpg?v=15 600w, ../assets/img/treatments/orthodontics-1200.jpg?v=15 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 48em) 92vw, 520px" alt="Braces in Deira at Pearlecent, Al Rigga" width="1200" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture></figure>
      <h2 data-reveal>How the visit works</h2>
      <ol class="land-steps" data-reveal><li><span>Book an orthodontic consultation.</span></li><li><span>The Orthodontic Specialist checks your teeth, bite and jaw, and may take X-rays and photos.</span></li><li><span>You get a treatment plan with the options, the expected time and the cost.</span></li><li><span>Your braces are fitted, or your aligners are given to you.</span></li><li><span>You come back for regular review visits.</span></li><li><span>When treatment ends, you wear a <a class="link-u" href="dentures-deira.html">retainer</a> to help keep your teeth in place.</span></li></ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="dbody land-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
  <div class="wrap land-faq__in">
    <div>
      <h2 id="faq-h" data-reveal>Questions about braces</h2>
      <div class="faq"><details data-reveal><summary>How long will I wear braces?</summary><p>It depends on how much your teeth need to move. The Orthodontic Specialist gives you an estimate after the consultation.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>Will braces feel sore?</summary><p>Teeth often feel sore for a few days after braces are fitted or adjusted. This usually settles. Soft food can help during these days.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>Can I choose clear aligners instead of braces?</summary><p>Clear aligners suit many cases, but not all. The Orthodontic Specialist will tell you if aligners are an option for you.</p></details><details data-reveal><summary>Can I pay in parts?</summary><p>You can split your payment into 4 with Tabby or Tamara. Ask our team for details when you book.</p></details></div>
    </div>
    <div class="land-visit" data-reveal>
      <h2>Visiting Pearlecent in Al Rigga</h2>
      <p>Pearlecent Shifah Medical Center is a family dental clinic in Deira, open since 2018. You can find us in Room 104, on the first floor of the Al Zarooni Building, 73 Al Rigga Road.</p>
      <p>We are open Saturday to Thursday from 9 AM to 10 PM, and on Friday from 1 PM to 9 PM. Your first general dental consultation is free. You can split your payment into 4 with Tabby or Tamara.</p>
      <p>Before any treatment, your dentist explains the benefits, the risks, the other options and the cost. You can ask questions and take time to decide.</p>
      <p><a class="link-u" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/LxxALHqsNsGpUrj29" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get directions</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
